Make qubes-setup-dnat-to-ns portable to systemd-less VMs (no systemd-resolved,
no python-dbus, no systemctl).

qubes-setup-dnat-to-ns runs on every NetVM/ProxyVM (qubes-core integration tests
invoke it from configure_netvm).  On a native Guix template using the Shepherd it
fails in three ways, each of which makes the whole script exit non-zero so that
configure_netvm fails and networking tests error in setUp:

1. `import dbus` raises ModuleNotFoundError when python-dbus is not installed,
   before the existing /etc/resolv.conf fallback in get_dns_resolved() can run.
   Make the import optional and, when absent, read /etc/resolv.conf directly.

2. get_dns_resolved() unconditionally calls dbus.SystemBus(); short-circuit to
   the resolv.conf fallback when dbus is unavailable.

3. The firewall reload uses "systemctl --no-block try-reload-or-restart
   qubes-firewall.service"; systemctl is absent, raising FileNotFoundError.
   Fall back to SIGHUP'ing the running qubes-firewall daemon, which it already
   handles as a rules reload (see qubesagent/firewall.py main()).

systemd distributions are unaffected: dbus imports, systemd-resolved answers, and
systemctl is present, so all original paths run unchanged and the fallbacks are
never reached.

Upstream: QubesOS/qubes-core-agent-linux, network/qubes-setup-dnat-to-ns.
Status: should-upstream (portable; only adds fallbacks for systemd-less VMs).
